<title>CHILE: Worker dies in Chile Chuquicamata plant accident.</title>
<headline>Worker dies in Chile Chuquicamata plant accident.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A worker died on Wednesday after being crushed in an accident at a molybdenum plant operated by state-owned Codelco's Chuquicamata copper mine, said a division spokesman.</p>
<p>The man, 20-year old Hector Sierra, fell into a mixing mill and was crushed around his hips and abdomen, he said.</p>
<p>Production at the plant was not affected by the accident.</p>
<p>Mining Minister Benjamin Teplizky has said the government is concerned about the sharp rise in fatal accidents in Chile's all-important mining industry this year.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
